      "prompt": "Prove algebraically that the sum of four consecutive integers is always even.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Let four consecutive integers be n, n + 1, n + 2 and n + 3.",
        "Write the given expression algebraically: n + (n + 1) + (n + 2) + (n + 3).",
        "Expand and simplify: n + (n + 1) + (n + 2) + (n + 3) = 4n + 6.",
        "Factorise/rearrange to expose the structure: 4n + 6 = 2(2n + 3).",
        "Since 4n + 6 factorises exactly to 2(2n + 3), the sum is always 2 times a whole number, so it is always even - though because 2n + 3 is itself always odd, the sum is NOT always a multiple of 4."
